  partName: Engine Block
  description: The Engine Block is situated at the middle-center-center of the rocket
    engine and is constructed from a robust Moteur material, which provides exceptional
    strength and durability. This large, complex-shaped component serves as the main
    structural element of the engine, housing the combustion chamber, fuel system,
    and other critical components. Notably, the engine block is designed to withstand
    immense forces and stresses generated by the combustion process, making it a
    vital part of the engine's overall architecture.
